# Keep LF in the repository regardless of the checkout platform. The shaders
# are include_str!'d into the binary, so line endings are build input.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sf2 binary
*.sfz text eol=lf
*.mid binary
*.wav binary

# The extracted comment text is browsable in the repository but is not part of
# a distribution: it is regenerated per release, the numbers are meaningless
# against any other version, and it doubles the size of a source download for
# something nobody building from source needs. `export-ignore` is what GitHub's
# generated "Source code" release assets honour; Cargo.toml's `exclude` covers
# `cargo package`.
/comments export-ignore
